@host = http://localhost:5003
@studentEmail = teststudent@example.com
@studentPassword = Test@12345

### 1. Log in as the student
# @name studentLogin
POST {{host}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{studentEmail}}", "password": "{{studentPassword}}" }

### 2. Ask the assistant. The reply streams as server-sent events (data: {"text":"..."} ... event: done).
# Insomnia may show the whole reply only when it has finished. To SEE it stream, use curl.exe -N (see MCP_STEP7_CAREER_ASSISTANT.md).
POST {{host}}/api/students/career-assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What skills am I missing and what should I learn first?",
  "history": []
}

### 3. A follow-up: the app sends the earlier turns back every time (the API stores nothing)
POST {{host}}/api/students/career-assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Which of those is the quickest to do?",
  "history": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "What skills am I missing and what should I learn first?" },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "(paste the reply from request 2 here)" }
  ]
}

### 4. Should return 400: empty message
POST {{host}}/api/students/career-assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "   " }

### 5. Should return 401: no token
POST {{host}}/api/students/career-assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "hello" }
